				"doc/readme.io/javascript-full-api-reference.md": {
					"diff": "--- published/doc/readme.io/javascript-full-api-reference.md\n+++ rebuilt/doc/readme.io/javascript-full-api-reference.md\n@@ -1,86 +1,297 @@\n----\n-category: 62ec0192a94ae90a45602b13\n-title: JavaScript Full API Reference\n----\n+## Classes\n \n+<a id=\"mixpanelgroup\"></a>\n \n-# mixpanel\n+### MixpanelGroup\n \n+Mixpanel Group Object\n \n-___\n-## mixpanel.add_group\n-Add a new group for this user.\n+#### Methods\n+\n+<a id=\"delete\"></a>\n+\n+##### delete()\n+\n+> **delete**(`callback?`): `any`\n+\n+Permanently delete a group.\n+\n+###### Parameters\n+\n+| Parameter | Type | Description |\n+| ------ | ------ | ------ |\n+| `callback?` | `Function` | If provided, the callback will be called after the tracking event |\n \n+###### Returns\n \n-### Usage:\n+`any`\n \n-```javascript\n- mixpanel.add_group('company', 'mixpanel')\n+###### Example\n+\n+```js\n+mixpanel.get_group('company', 'mixpanel').delete();\n ```\n \n+<a id=\"remove\"></a>\n \n+##### remove()\n \n-| Argument | Type | Description |\n-| ------------- | ------------- | ----- |\n-| **group_key** | <span class=\"mp-arg-type\">String</span></br></span><span class=\"mp-arg-required\">required</span> | Group key |\n-| **group_id** | <span class=\"mp-arg-type\">any</span></br></span><span class=\"mp-arg-required\">required</span> | A valid Mixpanel property type |\n-| **callback** | <span class=\"mp-arg-type\">Function</span></br></span><span class=\"mp-arg-optional\">optional</span> | If provided, the callback will be called after tracking the event. |\n+> **remove**(`list_name`, `value`, `callback?`): `any`\n \n+Remove a property from a group. The value will be ignored if doesn't exist.\n \n-___\n-## mixpanel.alias\n-The alias method creates an alias which Mixpanel will use to  remap one id to another. Multiple aliases can point to the  same identifier.\n+###### Parameters\n \n-The following is a valid use of alias:\n+| Parameter | Type | Description |\n+| ------ | ------ | ------ |\n+| `list_name` | `string` | Name of the property. |\n+| `value` | `Object` | Value to remove from the given group property |\n+| `callback?` | `Function` | If provided, the callback will be called after the tracking event |\n+\n+###### Returns\n \n+`any`\n \n-```javascript\n-mixpanel.alias('new_id', 'existing_id');\n-// You can add multiple id aliases to the existing ID\n-mixpanel.alias('newer_id', 'existing_id');\n+###### Example\n \n+```js\n+mixpanel.get_group('company', 'mixpanel').remove('Location', 'London');\n ```\n \n-Aliases can also be chained - the following is a valid example:\n+<a id=\"set\"></a>\n+\n+##### set()\n+\n+> **set**(`prop`, `to?`, `callback?`): `any`\n+\n+Set properties on a group.\n+\n+###### Parameters\n+\n+| Parameter | Type | Description |\n+| ------ | ------ | ------ |\n",
					"match": false,
					"packageHash": "3853db8ab05299a0ee92c50c112b7f951723918acab97550187934dd45e9fedc",
